Z||000008||MsBeth||06-22-2001||12:07 AM||||Totally get it ... Love the original movie, the newer version, the series on Disney a few years back (actually called Avonlea-about the next generation), and for those who didn't know they had a sequel shown on PBS a few months back - with the orginal cast members - It was great! <P>I think that the story touches a place in some people that miss the slower pace or the innocent nature and feel of it all.  It is an amazing coming of age story - that made me want to go directly to PEI (still want to- someday).  <P>MsBeth||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tweek||06-22-2001||05:22 AM||||When I was younger, I took a trip with my family to PEI. It was one of the best vacations Ive ever had. We visited the house that inspired the author, or the authors house, somethin like that. Beautiful island. That was one beach we went to that was like all smooth red sandstone. love it. <P>Anyways, that trip took us 3 cars to get there from Maine. Van blew its 2nd trans. (had a total of 4 diff ones before we sold it) Rented a car from "Rent-a-Wreck" And truct me, They aint kidding, that lasted 45 minutes, and we got a second one from them which ALSO had to visit the shop while in PEI, expensive, but fun.||||reg||1
